# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# The template too, since 2026-09-14. It sits beside the real .env with the
# same names and layout, and a key was typed into it once instead of into .env.
# Ignoring it means a filled-in copy can never be committed by accident. The
# cost is that a fresh clone has no template: the model settings are explained
# in backend/src/llm/provider.js, and `grep -rn process.env backend/src` lists
# every setting the server reads.
.env.example

